+## Forked query ownership
+
+`CacheSafeParams` contains the generation configuration, complete curated
+history, selected model, and configuration version. Each Config owns its
+snapshot together with the session ID; a different current session cannot read
+it. History containers are copied and retained parts remain intact.
+
+`runWithForkedChat` owns a distinct generation identity and the existing child
+transcript writer. The writer records the complete bootstrap before generation,
+requires durable assistant commitment, and retains failed reasoning and usage.
+The fork preserves the selected reasoning configuration and exact request sizing.
+A requested alternate route resolves through the shared model resolver.
+
+A provider may cache an equal rendered prefix. Cache availability, retention,
+and eviction are provider facts; sharing history does not guarantee a cache hit.
+
+## Acceptance failure boundary
+
+Acceptance copies overlay files and then awaits `GeminiClient.adoptHistory`.
+Each adopted message is recorded before entering live history. These two
+resources do not form an atomic transaction: a failed append can leave applied
+files and zero or partially adopted history. The overlay also suppresses some
+per-file copy and removal failures. Coordinated ownership and recoverable
+publication are required before atomic acceptance can be promised.
+
+The caller reports an acceptance failure, including the possibility of existing
+file/history changes, without resubmitting the prompt. Independent operation and
+cleanup errors remain observable. This failure handling does not close the
+transaction boundary.
 
