@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Invocation and artifact ownership behavioral test plan
+
+Operational constraints prohibit launching the CLI, contacting providers,
+submitting sessions, or building the application during this change. Verify the
+source using mocked boundaries and temporary fixture data. Do not interpret that
+verification as a live terminal or multi-day conversation test.
+
+- Drive batch, stream, exact-count, hook, goal, and daemon generation through a
+  main Config and overlapping child frames. Observe the actual raw provider and
+  OpenAI SDK request boundaries. Every request retains its correct owner.
+- Exercise both initial and resumed background child launch hooks. The hook,
+  factory, chat, and continuation share the spawning identity; the parent remains
+  unchanged across asynchronous child completion.
+- Select unsupported routes and invalid tokenizer URL forms. Observe no provider
+  call or configuration publication. Failed selection preserves the prior route.
+- Hold or reject initial provider preparation. Optional status reads preserve
+  absence while generation and required provider facts refuse. Reuse a utility
+  client through root, child and root frames; mocked generation and embedding
+  calls must resolve the active pair without retaining a child's provider.
+- Persist distinct/equal text and binary results concurrently from separate OS
+  fixture processes; reopen Config and contend at quota. Verify immutable bytes,
+  deduplication, quota accounting, durability errors, and old referenced files.
+- Approve edited and empty file content, including a new file and repeated edits.
+  Replay lookalike serialized parameters and verify they acquire no trusted
+  modification provenance.
+- Pass open/patterned external schemas and explicit reject-all schemas through
+  actual validation. Neither field coercion nor runtime-key bypass is allowed.
+- Feed missing terminal reasons and legitimate XML text alongside structured
+  calls. Verify retained text and incomplete status without executable text repair.
+
+After separate operational authorization, repeat applicable cases through the
+installed Linux terminal and headless renderers and exercise extended resume and
+compaction conversations. Do not launch those runs as part of this source task.
+
+- Record dispatch before a mocked provider call and finalize exactly once. Hold or
+  fail durable writes; observe no premature dispatch or usage publication. Keep
+  no request, served zero, finalized missing usage, and unfinalized dispatch
+  distinct through terminal JSON, ACP, SDK, web, and history projections.
+- Sum independently valid reports at and beyond the safe-integer boundary through
+  the real live metrics, retained history, ledger and export consumers. Verify refusal before publishing unsafe
+  totals and preserve missing, unfinalized, and reported-zero states in Markdown
+  and JSONL. Todo details retain only observed status timing across pause/reopen.
+- Serialize valid replay state across pages, including carried tool correlation
+  and Goal facts. Refuse malformed/versionless state before updates or cursor
+  publication. Preserve the original failure and every dangling-cleanup failure,
+  including falsy values, while clearing active-record attribution.
+- Repeat compaction with explicit original user/delegator parts, edits, media,
+  forks, retry, and resume. Require identical retained authored bytes outside each
+  structurally valid six-section summary. Refuse malformed snapshots and exact
+  size violations; do not claim semantic summary validation.
+- Exercise all nine terminal/headless/ACP writer contention directions using real
+  test-owned leases and mocked generation. Hold new/resume/rollback/shutdown
+  phases and verify owner admission, authoritative history, resource settlement,
+  and error identity. Cover source and destination ownership for mutations.
+- Hold session maintenance through mutation, target-state verification, scheduled
+  task changes and lease release. Fail each phase, including multiple and falsy
+  rejections. Repeat requests after task-update failure and verify repair.
+  Throw from error observers and diagnostic writers; retain every cause and
+  invoke each observer once. Inject early shutdown callback failure and verify
+  all independent callbacks, signal handlers and output obligations still settle.
+- Use the actual required recorder with temporary root and child transcripts.
+  Hold durable assistant append and verify calls cannot execute or terminate
+  successfully before it settles. Preserve failed/cancelled partial output and
+  last valid served usage; a poisoned writer cannot resume admission.
+- Feed real telemetry through status data and both terminal renderers. Change
+  sessions, same-label models, declared windows, and background observations;
+  reject old command callbacks and preserve root route outside child ALS frames.
+- Use actual output adapters and cleanup in test-owned Node children with private
+  AF_UNIX streams. Under backpressure, orderly exits must drain every callback
+  and byte, including registered cleanup writes. SIGKILL may leave a torn tail.
+  No child invokes the CLI, model, service, or harness.
+- Read a private copy of Test A's captured wire stream with the Rust scanner.
+  Retain valid owned full-usage observations, mark every unaccounted record, and
+  refuse complete certification. Include malformed middle records, invalid UTF-8,
+  missing final LF, duplicate/mismatched identity, and oversized physical records.
+- Apply the reviewed source patch to a pristine pinned checkout; require exact
+  resulting bytes and absences, idempotence, semantic relationships, and
+  transactional rollback for edits, additions, and deletions.
+
+Compaction and child reasoning by reference is unimplemented. Existing-source
+400 KB reasoning reproductions remain red and document that whole open finding.
+Do not treat artifact retention, orderly output draining, or partial wire
+observations as evidence that a reasoning reference can be recovered.
+
+Speculation acceptance remains non-atomic across workspace files and history.
+Actual temporary-overlay tests retain failing first/second append cases that
+leave applied files and zero/partial adopted history. Caller controls verify an
+explicit failure and no silent resubmission, without claiming atomicity.
+
+Review worktree lifetime correctness remains unimplemented. Source inspection
+identifies overwriteable per-PR leases, removal without prior-owner settlement,
+and suppressed inner cleanup failures. No concurrent runtime reproduction or
+cleanup qualification is claimed. Exclusive ownership must cover creation,
+review/probe/base trees, branches, associated files, and both cleanup entry points.
+
+Operational daemon metrics remain incorrect. The ring admits malformed or partial
+token observations, permits unsafe addition, and exposes mutable sampled buckets.
+The bridge suppresses accounting callback failures and fills missing counts with
+zero; the sampler also fills failed or absent readings with zero. A complete fix
+must coordinate observation admission, per-frame mutation, measurement failure
+and staleness, checked interval arithmetic, and immutable publication. Sampled
+operational readings are distinct from complete session generation accounting.
+That whole lifecycle remains open; the session summary corrections do not close
+it. Ten pure actual-source failures are retained outside the shipping tests; the
+bridge and sampler findings are source-confirmed, without runtime qualification.
+
+Prompt-hook failure policy remains open. Invalid model JSON/schema and operational
+failures currently allow continuation. Cancellation is inferred from message
+text, and the enclosing hook event bus reports failure without a blocking output
+for most event kinds. A correct policy must distinguish failed evaluation from a
+model decision and respect whether an event occurs before admission or after an
+irreversible action. The shared generation owner does not repair that policy.
+These paths are source-confirmed; existing fixtures preserve the current behavior,
+not a qualification of fail-closed operation.
+
+Resident background AgentTool disposal still exposes a void callback, and its
+unexpected asynchronous failures are logged without an owning caller joining
+them. Writer attachment is shared by all children, foreground forks are awaited,
+and explicit background forks use the same lifetime for every renderer. Ordinary
+child resource settlement and InProcessBackend settlement are awaited. The
+remaining resident-background disposal contract needs coordinated changes to the
+registry, continuation, caller shutdown, and failure publication; it is not closed
+by those narrower lifetime fixes.
+
