-
-## Command mode
-
-Command mode runs a shell command whose stdout is displayed in the status line. The command receives structured JSON context via stdin for session-aware output.
-
-### Prerequisites
-
-- [`jq`](https://jqlang.github.io/jq/) is recommended for parsing the JSON input (install via `brew install jq`, `apt install jq`, etc.)
-- Simple commands that don't need JSON data (e.g. `git branch --show-current`) work without `jq`
-
-### Configuration
-
-Add a `statusLine` object under the `ui` key in `~/.qwen/settings.json`:
+| Setting                | Meaning                                                                                                                                                        |
+| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`                 | `"preset"`                                                                                                                                                     |
+| `items`                | Selected item IDs, rendered in the built-in order with `\|` separators                                                                                         |
+| `useThemeColors`       | Apply the active theme; defaults to `true`                                                                                                                     |
+| `hideContextIndicator` | Explicitly show or hide the footer's separate context indicator; when absent, context presets hide duplicate information unless the layout needs the indicator |
+
+| Item                   | Meaning                                                             |
+| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `model-with-reasoning` | Selected model name and configured reasoning effort                 |
+| `model`                | Selected model name                                                 |
+| `git-branch`           | Git branch when available                                           |
+| `context-remaining`    | Configured window less the last served prompt, as a percentage      |
+| `context-used`         | Last served prompt divided by the configured window                 |
+| `total-input-tokens`   | Reported session input total, with missing/open observation counts  |
+| `total-output-tokens`  | Reported session output total, with missing/open observation counts |
+| `current-dir`          | Current execution directory                                         |
+| `project-name`         | Execution directory's basename                                      |
+| `pull-request-number`  | Open pull request for the branch, using `gh pr view`                |
+| `branch-changes`       | Recorded lines added and removed                                    |
+| `run-state`            | Ready, working, or confirmation state                               |
+| `qwen-version`         | CLI version                                                         |
+| `context-window-size`  | Configured model window                                             |
+| `used-tokens`          | Last provider-served prompt count                                   |
+| `session-id`           | Selected session identity                                           |
+
+The default selection contains `model-with-reasoning`, `git-branch`,
+`context-remaining`, `current-dir`, and `context-used`.
+
+The last served prompt describes a completed provider observation. It does not
+measure the next request after edits or compaction. `/context` measures the
+rendered request exactly. A served prompt can exceed a newly selected window;
+the displayed ratio preserves that fact and can exceed 100%. A genuine zero is
+shown. The ratio is absent when the prompt or configured window is unknown.
+
+Reported totals include all observed owners in the selected session, including
+children. Input is counted again on every served request. Output already includes
+reasoning; cached tokens are part of input. Missing reports and unfinalized
+observations remain explicit. No requests, no served reports, and reported zero
+have different displays.
+
+## Custom commands
+
+A command receives JSON on stdin and its stdout becomes the status line. Use a
+script for substantial formatting:
 
 ```json
 {
   "ui": {
     "statusLine": {
       "type": "command",
-      "command": "input=$(cat); model=$(echo \"$input\" | jq -r '.model.display_name'); pct=$(echo \"$input\" | jq -r '.context_window.used_percentage'); echo \"$model  ctx:${pct}%\""
+      "command": "bash ~/.qwen/statusline-command.sh",
+      "refreshInterval": 5,
+      "respectUserColors": false,
+      "hideContextIndicator": false
     }
   }
 }
 ```
 
-| Field                  | Type        | Required | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
-| ---------------------- | ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
-| `type`                 | `"command"` | Yes      | Must be `"command"`                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
-| `command`              | string      | Yes      | Shell command to execute. Receives JSON via stdin, stdout is displayed (up to 2 lines).                                                                                                                                  |
-| `refreshInterval`      | number      | No       | Re-run the command every N seconds (minimum 1). Useful for data that changes without an Agent state event (clock, quota, uptime).                                                                                        |
-| `respectUserColors`    | boolean     | No       | Preserve ANSI color codes in command output instead of applying dimmed footer styling. Defaults to `false`.                                                                                                              |
-| `hideContextIndicator` | boolean     | No       | Hide the built-in context usage indicator in the footer right section. Defaults to `false` — command output is not inspected for context information, so set it explicitly if your command already prints context usage. |
-
-### JSON input
-
-The command receives a JSON object via stdin with the following fields:
+`refreshInterval` is optional and must be at least one second. It refreshes
+external data such as a clock or quota independently of session events.
+`respectUserColors` preserves command ANSI colors when true. Set
+`hideContextIndicator` explicitly if the command already displays the context
+information you need.
+
